Cause: `mergePageConfigDocument` was always taking `normalizePageDocument(value)`’s component state. For config-only updates (no `state` provided), `normalizeLiveState` falls back to default live state, overwriting existing Select/Radio selections.

Fix (minimal + safe): in `lib/pageDocument/normalize.ts`, `mergePageConfigDocument` now detects whether the incoming update actually includes a valid `state` object for the component; if not, it preserves `baseComponent.state` while still applying the config changes.

